# Claims deliberately exempt from check-facts.py, each with its reason.
# An entry here is a decision, not a silencing: if you cannot write the reason,
# the claim needs an artifact instead.

# ARITHMETIC, and labelled as such in the text ("theoretical peak bandwidth"):
# 5.001 GHz memory clock x 256-bit bus / 8 x 2 (DDR) = 320.1 GB/s. The measured
# streaming-read figure for this part is 277 GB/s and was taken on the T4G
# sibling, not here -- the articles do not quote it as this rig's.
320.1

# ROUNDING of a value that IS in evidence: engine-startup.log records
# "Model loading took 9.8 GiB memory and 55.748559 seconds".
55.75
